# Testing Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define testing strategy, tools, and coverage expectations
- Ensure critical business logic and auth paths are tested
- Prevent regressions in billing, permissions, and data integrity

## Best Practices

- **Testing pyramid**: Many unit → fewer integration → critical E2E
- **Vitest** for unit and integration tests
- **React Testing Library** for component tests
- **Playwright** for E2E critical paths
- **MSW** for mocking external APIs in tests
- Test repositories with test database (Docker PostgreSQL)
- Colocate tests: `case.service.test.ts` next to `case.service.ts`
- Or `__tests__/` folder within feature

## Coding Standards

```typescript
// Unit test structure
describe('CaseService', () => {
  describe('create', () => {
    it('creates case with valid input', async () => { ... });
    it('rejects invalid clientId', async () => { ... });
    it('requires cases:create permission', async () => { ... });
  });
});
```

- AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert
- One assertion focus per test (logical grouping OK)
- Factory functions for test data in `tests/factories/`
- Clean database between integration tests

## Folder Structure

```
tests/
├── factories/           # Test data builders
├── helpers/             # Auth helpers, db setup
├── e2e/                 # Playwright specs
src/features/cases/
├── services/case.service.ts
└── services/case.service.test.ts
```

## Naming Convention

| Type | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Unit test file | `*.test.ts` |
| E2E spec | `*.spec.ts` |
| Test describe | Unit under test name |
| Test case | `it('should ...')` descriptive behavior |

## Performance Rules

- Unit tests must run <5s total per feature
- Parallelize Vitest workers
- E2E: run critical path only in CI (login, create case, invoice)

## Security Rules

- Test permission denial paths explicitly
- Test cross-tenant access returns 404/not found
- Never use production credentials in tests

## Coverage Targets

| Layer | Target |
|-------|--------|
| Services/Repositories | 80%+ |
| Server Actions | 70%+ |
| Utils | 90%+ |
| UI Components | 50%+ (critical paths) |
| E2E | Auth, CRUD cases, billing flow |

## Examples

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — Test cross-tenant isolation
it('returns null when case belongs to different org', async () => {
  const result = await caseRepository.findById(caseId, otherOrgId);
  expect(result).toBeNull();
});

// ✅ GOOD — Component test
it('shows empty state when no cases', () => {
  render(<CaseList cases={[]} isLoading={false} />);
  expect(screen.getByText(/no cases/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

## Things to Avoid

- Testing implementation details (internal state)
- Snapshot tests for entire pages ( brittle)
- Skipping auth/permission tests
- Flaky E2E without proper waits
- Tests depending on execution order

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Unit tests for new business logic
- [ ] Permission denial case tested
- [ ] Edge cases covered (empty, invalid input)
- [ ] Integration test if DB queries added
- [ ] E2E updated if critical user flow changed
- [ ] All tests pass locally
